      "side": 1,
      "message": "At present, I am not managing a pool of UNI Ids. It is only managing bounds checks on the range of UNI IDs for each ONU. The default being a range of 1 (0..0) for single-uni. If a Resource Profile is loaded with 0..255 it will support multi-uni. But, again, their is no pools to allocate at this time.\n\nIn the future, I think it might be able to support arbitrary pools. But, presently, OpenOLT still depends on a fixed logical port bit-encoded form. So, the pool of UNI IDs needs to wait for another refactoring effort.",
